WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:05.800
Apple Research found three regimes as task complexity increases:

2
00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:10.200
on simple tasks, standard models can outperform reasoning models;

3
00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:14.500
at medium complexity, extra reasoning helps;

4
00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:18.500
and at high complexity both can collapse.

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:24.500
Reasoning effort also stops scaling indefinitely: it rises with complexity up to a point and then falls, even with token budget available.

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:31.000
In an application with RAG, a browser or tools, the model processes content the user did not write.

7
00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
A malicious instruction can travel inside a retrieved webpage, document or API response.

8
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Greshake et al. showed that indirect prompt injection can manipulate the behavior of LLM-integrated applications

9
00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.200
and influence when or how other APIs are called.

10
00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:56.400
TabooRAG shows another route: a retrievable document can inject risk-relevant context into an otherwise benign query

11
00:00:56.400 --> 00:01:00.800
and trigger a refusal.

12
00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:06.500
The attack exploits shared alignment criteria to transfer blocking behavior across models.

13
00:01:06.500 --> 00:01:11.500
The risk here is not a harmful answer, but loss of availability.

14
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:18.200
Conformal Thinking reframes the reasoning budget as risk control:

15
00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:23.500
stop when confidence is sufficient

16
00:01:23.500 --> 00:01:28.700
and also cut off instances that appear unsolvable within the budget.

17
00:01:28.700 --> 00:01:35.300
The goal is not to spend every available token, but to satisfy a target error rate while using compute where it improves reliability.

18
00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:41.800
A robust agent limits permissions and validates external content

19
00:01:41.800 --> 00:01:46.800
while separating untrusted data from authoritative instructions.

20
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:51.000
Before an irreversible action, it adds an explicit verification boundary.

21
00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:56.000
It also sets hard budgets for time, tokens and tool calls, and keeps explicit fallbacks

22
00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.500
and can abstain. The goal is to bound damage when one layer fails.
